If the tunnel has closed, start a foreground tunnel and keep its terminal open:

```sh
ssh -N -L 127.0.0.1:14242:127.0.0.1:4242 marvin
```

Do not run a second tunnel if port 14242 is already occupied. The daemon still
listens only on `127.0.0.1:4242` on Marvin. No public or Tailscale HTTP listener
was added.

## Verified

- Running executable SHA256:
  `b00e0f8d52896e1084f0a04b52cd40d153fad8c9de5caafe3bdffdaa9e6e8f11`.
- Built from `edd8ce1` plus the reviewed, uncommitted dashboard changes. This is
  not a new source commit or push.
- Native Linux executable and current configuration checked before cutover.
- Migration tested on a private database copy, then applied to live storage.
- SQLite integrity check passed; all 36 Events, 36 Decisions, 36 Executions,
  and zero human labels were retained. Schema version is now 8; the migration
  adds indexes only.
- Journal source completed multiple successful polls after startup.
- All three notification rules remain shadowed; default remains ignore.
- Local and tunneled dashboard APIs, assets, and event detail passed checks.
  A real browser loaded the live page and detail without JavaScript errors.
- Plex, LFM2.5, Tailscale, SSH socket, and Hermes remained active.

The existing 36 Decisions include 33 successes and three timeouts. At deployment,
successful client request latency had a 61 ms median and 142 ms p95. These are
historical measurements, including synthetic checks, not a new benchmark or
GPU-only timing.

## Backup and recovery

Private backup directory on Marvin:

```text
/home/heath/mrmr-shadow/rollback/dashboard-20261026T020158Z-k7r0ging/
```

It contains the previous binary, configuration, service unit, an online backup,
and a final `mrmr.db` backup taken after the old process stopped. `manifest.json`
records hashes, counts, and deployment checks. `validation.db` is a separate
migrated copy used before cutover.

Do not run the old binary against schema 8, or overwrite the live database with
this backup after new events arrive. A rollback needs a separate data-preserving
plan. None was performed during deployment.

## Remaining limits

The new timing log runs after each stored Decision. No new real event arrived
during verification, so a live post-upgrade timing line is still pending. The
logging path passed an offline native-d1 protocol test; no synthetic record was
added to the real dataset to force a log line.

The dashboard cannot alert independently when mrmr is down. Poll health resets
on restart; stale model history does not prove current model availability.
The SSH tunnel must remain connected to view the page from this Mac.
